      "loadUpProtocol": "The Load-Up / Cadence: Start directly from the lower turnaround (knees extended) with feet and ankles relaxed. Patiently build pressure into the roller pads over 3–5 seconds (cue: *\"gradually bend your knees and dent the roller pad\"*) to crack the stack. Once moving, maintain a smooth 6-second concentric, 6-second eccentric cadence. Keep the feet and ankles relaxed upon load-up and during the first two repetitions to isolate the hamstrings. From the third repetition onward, instruct the client to actively dorsiflex their ankles during the concentric phase (cue: *\"pull your feet up to your knees\"*) to engage the gastrocnemius (calf) for added mechanical leverage and a tighter contraction. At the upper turn (fully contracted position), instruct the client to relax their ankles *before* initiating the eccentric phase (cue: *\"relax the ankles, THEN ease out\"*). Relaxing the ankles must take place while the weight arm is still, before beginning to lower the weight.",
